1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,729
Is water wet?

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,796
Pour water on a dry towel,
and the towel gets wet.

3
00:00:06,796 --> 00:00:07,506
Easy.

4
00:00:08,117 --> 00:00:10,167
But what about the water itself?

5
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:15,267
In science, wetting is what happens
when a liquid meets a surface.

6
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:17,701
Water sticks to other things.

7
00:00:17,701 --> 00:00:18,712
That's adhesion.

8
00:00:18,712 --> 00:00:20,293
It also sticks to itself.

9
00:00:20,293 --> 00:00:21,655
That's cohesion.

10
00:00:22,283 --> 00:00:25,393
If the pull of the surface
wins, water spreads.

11
00:00:25,393 --> 00:00:27,066
If not, it beads up.

12
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,959
So by that rule,
water isn't wet.

13
00:00:29,959 --> 00:00:32,089
It makes other things wet.

14
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,271
But dictionaries split.

15
00:00:34,271 --> 00:00:37,003
One says wet can mean
made up of liquid.

16
00:00:37,003 --> 00:00:39,197
By that rule, water is wet.

17
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:43,014
Our verdict? Wet is what happens to the dry thing.
